(4843191, 699616, 77192, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot and highly underrated. Nice DOF.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by my good friend salmiakki:</b></div><hr/><i>It has a nice rural French feel to it.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Couldn''t have put it better myself.</td>', 'Excellent shot and highly underrated. Nice DOF. Originally posted by my good friend salmiakki:It has a nice rural French feel to it.  Couldn''t have put it better myself.', '2008-07-24 16:59:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4843222, 699608, 77192, '<td valign="top">Saw this in voting and though it was yours Enzo. This is highly underrated (I can''t believe mine finished higher) I think part of the problem is geography - I didn''t know what a Friand was until I googled it and I wonder how many voters were the same. :-( Now I know, I want to try one lol.<br/> <br/>This image looks great though. I have to agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=29011" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Techo</a> about the way you always make your food shots look natural, arranging the table decorations/wine etc around the shot and somehow makng it look casual, almost effortless, and not at all "stagey" and artificial. Your use of DOF really adds to that - I don''t agree with the commenter who criticised it, I think it''s perfect here. The only technical criticism I''d make is the topping on the Friands seems a bit bright - not quite blown out but a bit bright for my taste nonetheless. I''m not too sure about the lemons but as I don''t know the dish I shan''t criticise ;-)<br/> <br/>Perhaps this isn''t your best shot but then you have very high standards. I can''t emphasise that last sentence enough. Keep it up Enzo, more food pics please :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-24 16:16:58.</i></td>', 'Saw this in voting and though it was yours Enzo. This is highly underrated (I can''t believe mine finished higher) I think part of the problem is geography - I didn''t know what a Friand was until I googled it and I wonder how many voters were the same. :-( Now I know, I want to try one lol. This image looks great though. I have to agree with  Techo about the way you always make your food shots look natural, arranging the table decorations/wine etc around the shot and somehow makng it look casual, almost effortless, and not at all "stagey" and artificial. Your use of DOF really adds to that - I don''t agree with the commenter who criticised it, I think it''s perfect here. The only technical criticism I''d make is the topping on the Friands seems a bit bright - not quite blown out but a bit bright for my taste nonetheless. I''m not too sure about the lemons but as I don''t know the dish I shan''t criticise ;-) Perhaps this isn''t your best shot but then you have very high standards. I can''t emphasise that last sentence enough. Keep it up Enzo, more food pics please :-)', '2008-07-24 17:16:16.000000', '2008-07-24 17:16:58.000000', 0),
